{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And if the appearance be not deeper than the skin.</b> Even though they said (Shevuot 6a) that every white appearance is deep — like the appearance of the sun, which is deeper than the shade — nevertheless, since the skin too has some degree of whiteness, not every white would count as deep relative to it, unless it passes the boundary of the skin's whiteness, so that the whiteness of the skin bears the same relation to it as the shade bears to the sun."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:11.320279834Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}